From 3698d1d7f46516374c66082ffbfa321afecbb7d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:19:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06922/11362] [outer-loop] ls20: L7 SOLVED, FULL GAME CLEAR
 (round 9, codex)

Round-9 gpt-5.6-sol session solved L7 on the first attempt, and it
turned out to be the final level. L7 introduces fog of war around a
single target requiring internal tuple (0,3,2); the counter now
drains 2 per attempted move (including blocked ones, up from 1).
Three directional pusher objects partition the maze into
otherwise-disconnected regions as forced one-way transports, not
tuple controls. Rotation is set by synchronizing with a moving
pinwheel; color and shape use static controls entered multiple times
modulo their cycle length.

Won live at action 672 with GameState.WIN. The source agent's own
reproduction_verified is honestly false (budget ran out after the
win), but the outer loop independently re-verified regardless: 5x
fresh env.reset() + replay via a new resolver priority branch, all 5
confirmed level=7, state=GameState.WIN. ls20 is fully solved.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: ls20 levels_reproduced 6 -> 7,
full_game_clear: true, final_game_state: GameState.WIN.
reproducible_total_levels 169 -> 170 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
